-- title:
--   Cubic space budget for the complete local-cover layout
-- statement:
--   Let $h,B,b\in\mathbb N$ and put $L=512h$. Let $v,p,c,R,T$ respectively denote the concrete vertex count, selected prime, bucket cap, candidate-assignment count, and schedule length. Assume $B\ge1$ and that $L+1$, $v+1$, $p+1$, $c+1$, $R+1$, $T+1$, $p^{2L+1}+1$, and $2^{L+1}+1$ are all at most $B$. For the local-cover layout starting at address $b$, its declared end address satisfies
--
--   $$
--   S_{\mathrm{cover}}(b,h)\le b+20B^3.
--   $$
--
--   The layout includes masks, decoded maps, raw values, histograms, the candidate matrix, scratch space, and gathered schedule rows.
--
--   This packages all these regions into one polynomial space estimate, so later callers can supply a single sufficient memory limit.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LightLocalCoverResources.lean#L90-L145

